What is Poultry Vaccines?
Poultry vaccines are formulated to induce an immune response that protects flocks from viral, bacterial, and parasitic pathogens that can cause severe morbidity, mortality, and economic loss. By targeting diseases such as Newcastle disease, avian influenza, Marek’s disease, salmonellosis, and coccidiosis, these biologics enable producers to maintain high bio‑security standards, reduce reliance on therapeutic antibiotics, and meet consumer expectations for safe, high‑quality protein.
